<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/undated">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Siege</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexander's siege of Gaza</h1><p class="enc-meta">Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wars-of-alexander-the-great">Wars of Alexander the Great</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexander's siege of Gaza was a siege by the army of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-the-great">Alexander the Great</a> in 332 BCE, following the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tyre">Tyre</a>, as he advanced towards <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/egypt">Egypt</a>. The city's Persian garrison resisted for some months before it was taken by storm. Its fall opened the way to Egypt for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/macedonian-empire">Macedonian Empire</a>.</p></div>
